  "result": "The quote now prints 27.06.\n\n**Root cause:** `to_cents` in `shop/money.py` padded the decimal part on the wrong side. `\"12.5\"` has the fraction `\"5\"`, and `rjust(2, \"0\")` turned it into `\"05\"`. So 12.50 was read as 12.05. Using `ljust` makes `\"5\"` become `\"50\"`, which is correct.\n\n**Tests:** pytest isn't installed, so I ran the suite with `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests -t .`. All 6 tests pass.\n\nI didn't add a regression test for single-decimal prices like `12.5`.",
